---
import SectionHead from './ui/SectionHead.astro';

interface Props {
  num?: string;
}

const { num = '11' } = Astro.props;
---

<section id="architecture" class="arch-section">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHead num={num} kicker="Architecture" title="How It Runs">
      <p>
        You never need to know any of this to use Abject. It's here for the engineers who want
        to know how it works, and why it's so hard to kill.
      </p>
    </SectionHead>

    <!-- Strata: the three tiers as layers, surface on top, containment as bedrock -->
    <div class="strata">
      <div class="stratum s-surface">
        <span class="s-num" aria-hidden="true">I</span>
        <div class="s-head">
          <h3>The Surface</h3>
          <p class="s-tag">The part you can see.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="s-body">A thin browser client. It draws the canvas and sends your input down. Nothing runs here. It only shows what the depths send up.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="seam"><span class="seam-label"><span aria-hidden="true">&#8597;</span> WS :7719</span></div>

      <div class="stratum s-depths">
        <span class="s-num" aria-hidden="true">II</span>
        <div class="s-head">
          <h3>The Depths</h3>
          <p class="s-tag">Where the abjects live.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="s-body">The MessageBus, Registry, Factory, Negotiator, Supervisor, LLM, ProxyGenerator and HealthMonitor. Every system service is an abject, with the same kind of manifest, the same messages and the same contracts. It is built as a bunch of objects communicating with each other, Smalltalk or Erlang style. Each one has a bounded mailbox and handles one message at a time, and supervisors restart the ones that die. And each one has an <em>ask</em> handler.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="seam"><span class="seam-label"><span aria-hidden="true">&#8597;</span> WorkerBridge</span></div>

      <div class="stratum s-containment">
        <span class="s-num" aria-hidden="true">III</span>
        <div class="s-head">
          <h3>The Containment</h3>
          <p class="s-tag">Code the LLM writes runs in a sandbox.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="s-body">A pool of worker threads. Generated JavaScript runs in a locked-down interpreter with no access of its own to the filesystem, the network or the process. Abjects written in other languages run as WebAssembly and can only import the capabilities they were given. An abject reaches the outside world only through capability objects, and only the ones you granted.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- The layer cake: the diagram as hero, straight on the void -->
    <div class="arch-cake">
      <div class="cake-head">
        <div>
          <p class="cake-kicker"><span class="cake-square" aria-hidden="true">&#9632;</span> Inside the depths</p>
          <h3>The Layers Inside</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="arch-cake-intro">Inside the depths there are three layers. On top are your workspaces. Each one is kept apart from the others and has its own abjects. Under them is a shared layer of system abjects. Everything talks through one MessageBus at the bottom.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cake-stage">
        <div class="cake-scroll">
            <svg class="cake-svg" viewBox="0 0 720 540" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Abject's layered architecture: workspaces on top, system abjects in the middle, and a single MessageBus at the base">
              <defs>
                <marker id="cake-flow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto">
                  <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="#5be5a0" fill-opacity="0.8"/>
                </marker>
              </defs>

              <!-- Tier 3 label -->
              <text class="lbl" x="40" y="22">// WORKSPACES (isolated)</text>

              <!-- Workspace A -->
              <rect class="ws" x="40" y="35" width="310" height="175"/>
              <rect class="ws-band" x="40" y="35" width="310" height="30"/>
              <text class="ws-title" x="58" y="56">workspace: default</text>
              <text class="obj" x="60" y="90">Chat</text>
              <text class="obj" x="60" y="112">ScrumMaster</text>
              <text class="obj" x="60" y="134">GoalManager &middot; TupleSpace</text>
              <text class="obj" x="60" y="156">KnowledgeBase</text>
              <text class="obj" x="60" y="178">SkillRegistry &middot; Theme</text>
              <text class="obj-note" x="60" y="200">+ Scheduler, JobManager, WebAgent, ...</text>

              <!-- Workspace B -->
              <rect class="ws" x="370" y="35" width="310" height="175"/>
              <rect class="ws-band" x="370" y="35" width="310" height="30"/>
              <text class="ws-title" x="388" y="56">workspace: research</text>
              <text class="obj" x="390" y="90">Chat</text>
              <text class="obj" x="390" y="112">ScrumMaster</text>
              <text class="obj" x="390" y="134">GoalManager &middot; TupleSpace</text>
              <text class="obj" x="390" y="156">WebBrowserViewer</text>
              <text class="obj" x="390" y="178">KnowledgeBase</text>
              <text class="obj-note" x="390" y="200">each workspace has its own abjects</text>

              <!-- Down arrows: Workspaces to System tier (living flows, no filter) -->
              <g class="flow">
                <line x1="255" y1="212" x2="255" y2="252"/>
                <line x1="300" y1="212" x2="300" y2="252"/>
                <line x1="340" y1="212" x2="340" y2="252"/>
                <line x1="430" y1="212" x2="430" y2="252"/>
                <line x1="520" y1="212" x2="520" y2="252"/>
                <line x1="610" y1="212" x2="610" y2="252"/>
              </g>

              <!-- Tier 2 label -->
              <text class="lbl" x="40" y="242">// SYSTEM ABJECTS (shared)</text>

              <!-- Tier 2: System Abjects band -->
              <rect class="sys" x="40" y="255" width="640" height="100"/>
              <text class="sys-t" x="360" y="287" text-anchor="middle">Registry &middot; Factory &middot; LLMObject &middot; ObjectCreator &middot; ProxyGenerator</text>
              <text class="sys-t" x="360" y="312" text-anchor="middle">Negotiator &middot; HealthMonitor &middot; WorkspaceManager &middot; Supervisor</text>
              <text class="sys-t" x="360" y="337" text-anchor="middle">Identity &middot; PeerRegistry &middot; PermissionBroker &middot; SkillRegistry</text>

              <!-- Down arrows: System to MessageBus -->
              <g class="flow">
                <line x1="280" y1="357" x2="280" y2="397"/>
                <line x1="360" y1="357" x2="360" y2="397"/>
                <line x1="440" y1="357" x2="440" y2="397"/>
                <line x1="520" y1="357" x2="520" y2="397"/>
                <line x1="600" y1="357" x2="600" y2="397"/>
              </g>

              <!-- Tier 1 label -->
              <text class="lbl" x="40" y="387">// MESSAGEBUS (shared by all)</text>

              <!-- Tier 1: MessageBus band, the key element in red -->
              <rect class="bus-shadow" x="46" y="406" width="640" height="90"/>
              <rect class="bus" x="40" y="400" width="640" height="90"/>
              <line class="bus-rule" x1="60" y1="416" x2="660" y2="416"/>
              <line class="bus-rule" x1="60" y1="474" x2="660" y2="474"/>
              <text class="bus-t" x="360" y="446" text-anchor="middle">MessageBus</text>
              <text class="bus-sub" x="360" y="465" text-anchor="middle">every message between two abjects goes through here</text>

              <!-- Caption -->
              <text class="cap" x="360" y="525" text-anchor="middle">workspaces are kept apart. everything under them is shared.</text>
            </svg>

        </div>
        <p class="pan-hint" aria-hidden="true">scroll the diagram sideways &#9654;</p>
        <p class="arch-note">The layers are just a way to think about it. The MessageBus doesn't know what a "system abject" is. Everything is an abject sending messages.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* ── Strata: full-width bands stacked like layers of rock ── */
  .strata {
    margin-bottom: 6.5rem;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--bone);
  }

  .stratum {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 6.5rem minmax(0, 4fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: 1rem 2.25rem;
    align-items: start;
    padding: 1.7rem 1.75rem;
  }

  .s-num {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 3.6rem;
    line-height: 0.85;
    color: var(--red);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .stratum h3 {
    font-size: 1.7rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .s-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--bone-meta);
  }

  .s-body {
    color: var(--bone-2);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .s-body em { color: var(--bone-heading); font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; }

  /* Surface: the thin top layer. */
  .s-surface { background: var(--panel-2); padding-block: 1.4rem; }

  /* Depths: the thick red layer where everything lives. */
  .s-depths {
    background: var(--red);
    padding-block: 2.6rem 2.8rem;
  }

  .s-depths .s-num { color: #16130f; font-size: 5rem; }
  .s-depths h3 { color: var(--on-red); font-size: 2.3rem; }
  .s-depths .s-tag { color: rgba(246, 239, 219, 0.85); }
  .s-depths .s-body { color: var(--on-red); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .s-depths .s-body em { color: var(--on-red); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 2px; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

  /* Containment: hatched bedrock with a heavy floor. */
  .s-containment {
    background:
      repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg, rgba(231, 225, 206, 0.05) 0 1px, transparent 1px 10px),
      var(--sunken);
    border-bottom: 6px solid var(--rule-strong);
    padding-block: 2rem 2.2rem;
  }

  /* A seam between layers: the channel that crosses it, labelled on the boundary. */
  .seam {
    position: relative;
    height: 0;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .seam-label {
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(6.5rem + 4rem);
    top: 0;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--living);
    background: var(--void);
    border: 1px solid rgba(91, 229, 160, 0.55);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* ── The layer cake ── */
  .cake-head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: 1rem 3rem;
    align-items: end;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .cake-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--bone-meta);
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }

  .cake-square { color: var(--red); margin-right: 0.35rem; }

  .arch-cake h3 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.4rem); }

  .arch-cake-intro {
    color: var(--bone-2);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .cake-stage {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 15rem;
    gap: 0 2.5rem;
    align-items: end;
  }

  .cake-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }

  .cake-svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 600px;
    height: auto;
  }

  .arch-note {
    max-width: 44ch;
    margin: 0 0 4.5rem;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--red);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--bone-meta);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .pan-hint {
    display: none;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--bone-meta);
    text-align: right;
  }

  .cake-svg .lbl { fill: var(--bone-meta); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; }
  .cake-svg .ws { fill: var(--sunken); stroke: var(--rule-strong); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-dasharray: 6 3; }
  .cake-svg .ws-band { fill: var(--band); }
  .cake-svg .ws-title { fill: var(--bone-3); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .cake-svg .obj { fill: var(--bone); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; }
  .cake-svg .obj-note { fill: var(--bone-meta); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; font-style: italic; }
  .cake-svg .flow line { stroke: var(--living); stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-opacity: 0.7; marker-end: url(#cake-flow); }
  .cake-svg .sys { fill: var(--panel); stroke: var(--bone); stroke-opacity: 0.55; stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .cake-svg .sys-t { fill: var(--bone); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 14px; }
  .cake-svg .bus-shadow { fill: #000; }
  .cake-svg .bus { fill: var(--red); }
  .cake-svg .bus-rule { stroke: var(--on-red); stroke-opacity: 0.35; stroke-width: 0.75; }
  .cake-svg .bus-t { fill: var(--on-red); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 24px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .cake-svg .bus-sub { fill: var(--on-red); fill-opacity: 0.85; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; }
  .cake-svg .cap { fill: var(--bone-meta); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; font-style: italic; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .stratum { grid-template-columns: 4.5rem minmax(0, 1fr); padding-inline: 1.25rem; }
    .s-body { grid-column: 2; }
    .s-num { font-size: 2.8rem; }
    .s-depths .s-num { font-size: 3.6rem; }
    .seam-label { left: calc(4.5rem + 2.5rem); }
    .cake-head { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .cake-stage { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .arch-note { margin: 1.25rem 0 0 auto; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .pan-hint { display: block; }
    .arch-note { margin-left: 0; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .stratum { grid-template-columns: 3rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0.75rem 1rem; padding-inline: 1rem; }
    .s-num { font-size: 2.2rem; }
    .s-depths .s-num { font-size: 2.8rem; }
    .s-depths h3 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
    .stratum h3 { font-size: 1.45rem; }
    .seam-label { left: 4rem; }
  }
</style>
